# Story page: intro
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = Once, in a garden
---
If you are hoping for a story in which a small snake finds happiness, contentment and a pleasant place to nap, I must ask you to close this game at once. This is not that story.

This is the story of a snake who lived in a garden, a word which here means 'a patch of grass with one apple in it and a great many things waiting to go wrong.'

Now and then, at the corner of its eye, something shimmered. The snake ignored it, which is what everyone does with a warning until it is far too late to do anything else.

You have named the snake {name}. It is a fine name, and I am sorry to say it will appear in some very unfortunate sentences.
